IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oasda-witnesses`

-- Oaths, Affidavits and Statutory Declarations Act 2005 (WA), with Criminal Code (WA) s 169 -- the Q&A layer: the
-- questions people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters.
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every exported question takes
-- `my role` first ("Which of these describes you"). A question about another role answers `does not arise for you`
-- without reading any other input, so the site's question form never asks those inputs and drops the question.
--
-- ROLES. The baseline (oasda-witnesses.l4) already has the Act's two seats, and they are the two roles here:
--   - the person making a statutory declaration or an affidavit (the declarant or deponent): s 5, s 11, ss 12 and 16,
--     ss 14 and 15, the remote and electronic question, and Criminal Code s 169;
--   - the person asked to witness one: Schedule 2 and s 12(6), ss 8, 9(6)-(8) and 10(5), s 13, s 17, and the remote
--     and electronic question.
-- The court, the chief judicial officer who appoints court authorised witnesses (s 10) and the translator (s 14) are
-- not seats: what they do appears as what it means for the maker or the witness.
--
-- SITUATION (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act encoding). One situation input, shared by both roles with one name,
-- type and @desc, so the form asks it once: `the document` (`Document`: a statutory declaration, or an affidavit). The
-- Act's rules divide by it: Part 3 (ss 8-10) is affidavits, Part 4 (ss 11, 12) statutory declarations. It is placed
-- straight after `my role`, and a question about the other document answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else:
--   - the maker: s 5 (affirming instead of swearing) arises for an affidavit; s 11 and the s 12 validity question for a
--     statutory declaration;
--   - the witness: Schedule 2 item 20 ("a lawyer") and s 12(6) for a statutory declaration; s 8 and ss 9(6)-(8), 10(5)
--     for an affidavit.
-- Criminal Code s 169 sets a different maximum for each document, so the maker's maximum-penalty question takes the
-- same input as its fact, and arises for both values. The questions that apply alike to both documents (ss 13, 14, 15,
-- 17, s 169's elements, and the remote and electronic question) take no situation input.
--
-- The rules are in oasda-witnesses.l4. This module calls them and restates none. For each role, where the situation
-- holds, each answer is the baseline export's own, wrapped in a type that can also say `does not arise for you`. No
-- exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Oaths, Affidavits and Statutory Declarations Act 2005 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit`
    `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

-- The situation: which document. Read only through the helpers below, which list every value and have no OTHERWISE
-- (graffiti finding 31).
DECLARE `Document` IS ONE OF
    `a statutory declaration`
    `an affidavit`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `imprisonment for months` HAS `the number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Declaration witness answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `as a witness of this declaration I am` HAS `my standing for the declaration` IS A `My standing as a statutory declaration witness`

DECLARE `Affidavit witness answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `as a witness of this affidavit I am` HAS `my standing for the affidavit` IS A `My standing as an affidavit witness`

DECLARE `Validity answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `my declaration is` HAS `how it stands` IS A `How my statutory declaration stands`

DECLARE `Remote answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the Act says` HAS `what it says` IS A `What this Act says about doing it remotely`

DECLARE `Admissibility answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `for ss 14 and 15` HAS `what ss 14 and 15 say` IS A `Admissibility under ss 14 and 15`

DECLARE `Penalty answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the most is` HAS `the most I face` IS A `Most I face`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

§§ `The situations a question arises in`

GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration situation does not hold` IF
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `a statutory declaration` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an affidavit` THEN TRUE

GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the affidavit situation does not hold` IF
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `a statutory declaration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an affidavit` THEN FALSE

-- Criminal Code s 169 sets its maximum by the document: (2) a statutory declaration, (1) a statement on oath, which an
-- affidavit is.
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Document`
GIVETH A `Kind of document`
`the s 169 kind of` `the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the document`
    WHEN `a statutory declaration` THEN `my statutory declaration`
    WHEN `an affidavit` THEN `my affidavit, sworn or affirmed`

§§ `For the person making a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

§§§ `ss 5, 11, 12, 16 -- making it`

@export May I affirm instead of swearing an oath for my affidavit (s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I affirm instead of swearing for my affidavit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the affidavit situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `May I affirm instead of swearing`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I make a WA statutory declaration about any matter, at any time, for any purpose (s 11)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I make a statutory declaration about any matter, at any time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the declaration situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` `May I make a statutory declaration about any matter`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my WA statutory declaration validly made (ss 12, 16)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
      `my declaration` IS A `Statutory declaration` @desc How your declaration was prepared, declared and witnessed
GIVETH A `Validity answer`
`Is my statutory declaration valid` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the declaration situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `my declaration is` (`Is my statutory declaration validly made` `my declaration`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 14, 15 -- will a court accept it`

@export Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my affidavit or statutory declaration?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the maker or witness signed with a rubber stamp` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a stamp was used to make a signature or mark (not merely to imprint a name)
      `it is in a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the affidavit or declaration is in a language other than English
      `it has a qualified translation and translator's affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a suitably qualified translator translated it into written English and made an affidavit with the translation attached
GIVETH AN `Admissibility answer`
`Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting my document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `for ss 14 and 15` (`Do ss 14 and 15 stop a court accepting it` `the maker or witness signed with a rubber stamp` `it is in a language other than English` `it has a qualified translation and translator's affidavit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Criminal Code s 169 -- a false statement in it`

@export Do I commit a crime under Criminal Code s 169 by what I said in my affidavit or declaration?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I made a statement in it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you made the statement in your affidavit or statutory declaration
      `the statement is false in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement is false in a material particular
      `I knew it was false` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew the statement was false when you made it
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit the s 169 crime by what I said` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `yes if` (`Do I commit the false statement crime` `I made a statement in it` `the statement is false in a material particular` `I knew it was false`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- Both documents carry a maximum, so the question arises for both values of the document; the value is its fact.
@export What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement in my affidavit or declaration (Criminal Code s 169)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`What is the most I face for a knowingly false statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `the most is` (`What is the most I face for a false statement` (`the s 169 kind of` `the document`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit`

§§§ `Schedule 2, s 12(6) -- witnessing a statutory declaration`

@export Am I a "lawyer" within item 20 of Schedule 2, for witnessing a statutory declaration (Interpretation Act s 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
      `I have been admitted to the Australian legal profession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted as a lawyer in any Australian jurisdiction
      `I hold a current Australian practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate now
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I a lawyer for Schedule 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the declaration situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I a lawyer` `I have been admitted to the Australian legal profession` `I hold a current Australian practising certificate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I witness this WA statutory declaration, and on what footing (s 12(6), Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
      `me, as a declaration witness` IS A `Statutory declaration witness` @desc Where the declaration is made and who you are
GIVETH A `Declaration witness answer`
`May I witness this statutory declaration, and how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the declaration situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `as a witness of this declaration I am` (`May I witness this statutory declaration` `me, as a declaration witness`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 8, 9(6)-(8), 10(5) -- witnessing an affidavit`

@export Am I an "experienced legal practitioner", for witnessing an affidavit (s 8)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
      `I have been admitted to the Australian legal profession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been admitted as a lawyer in any Australian jurisdiction
      `I hold a current Australian practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate now
      `years I have been a legal practitioner` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years, up to now, you have continuously been a lawyer holding a current practising certificate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an experienced legal practitioner for affidavits` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the affidavit situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Am I an experienced legal practitioner` `I have been admitted to the Australian legal profession` `I hold a current Australian practising certificate` `years I have been a legal practitioner`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I witness this affidavit, and on what footing (ss 8, 9(6)-(8), 10(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the document` IS A `Document` @desc Which document it is: a statutory declaration (Part 4) or an affidavit (Part 3)
      `me, as an affidavit witness` IS A `Affidavit witness` @desc Where the affidavit is made, who you are, and whether you were involved in it
GIVETH AN `Affidavit witness answer`
`May I witness this affidavit, and how` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN
        IF `the affidavit situation does not hold` `the document`
        THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `as a witness of this affidavit I am` (`May I witness this affidavit` `me, as an affidavit witness`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 13, 17 -- my duties and the offence`

@export As the witness, must I read the document aloud, check it was understood, and certify that on it (s 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the maker is blind or illiterate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person making the affidavit or declaration is blind or illiterate
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I read the document aloud and certify it` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `yes if` (`Must I read it aloud and certify` `the maker is blind or illiterate`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Do I commit the s 17 offence of pretending to be an authorised witness?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am an authorised witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in fact an authorised witness for the affidavit or declaration
      `I pretended or asserted that I am one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you pretended, or asserted, that you are an authorised witness
      `I knew I was not one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew you were not an authorised witness
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit the offence of pretending to be an authorised witness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `yes if` (`Do I commit the pretending offence` `I am an authorised witness` `I pretended or asserted that I am one` `I knew I was not one`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for pretending to be an authorised witness (s 17)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest imprisonment for pretending to be an authorised witness` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `imprisonment for months` `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for pretending in months`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For both: witnessing remotely, and rubber stamps`

§§§ `ss 7(3), 9(3)(c), 12(3)(c), 15(2)`

@export Does this Act let me do this by audio or video link, or electronically (ss 7(3), 9(3)(c), 12(3)(c))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what I want to do` IS A `Kind of act` @desc What you want to do remotely or electronically
GIVETH A `Remote answer`
`Does the Act let me do this remotely or electronically` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `the Act says` (`Does the Act let me do it remotely` `what I want to do`)
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `the Act says` (`Does the Act let me do it remotely` `what I want to do`)

-- s 15(2) speaks of "a person" making a signature or mark on the document, the maker and the witness alike.
@export May I use a rubber stamp to imprint my name beside my signature (s 15(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I stamp my name beside my signature on the document` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am making a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `yes if` `May I stamp my name beside my signature`
    WHEN `I am asked to witness a statutory declaration or an affidavit` THEN `yes if` `May I stamp my name beside my signature`
